                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue
                ]","reason":"The current nested node constraint only requires a QuantityValue class and no longer constrains the shell inclination to the source-required value of 7 degrees. The removed value and unit property shapes were the candidate's only constraints expressing that condition.","expected":"The boundary point's shell inclination quantity must represent 7 degrees from horizontal, using the declared quantity representation.","suggestion":"Restore nested constraints for qudt:value and qudt:unit, including the required value and degree unit constraints.","evidence_excerpt":"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shellInclinationAngle> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> "The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where the shell is inclined 7 deg from horizontal." ."},{"issue_id":"d188b42d0a0b569fdcb53a423cd0303dc37e596b81dd4fd0598f3ab3459e4686","category":"SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR","source_clause":"I2.2.5","exact_source_excerpt":"I2.2.5 The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where
         the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.","exact_candidate_excerpt":"sh:node [
                    a sh:NodeShape ;
                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue
                ]","reason":"The candidate no longer constrains qudt:value to the declared canonical decimal serialization. The supplied representation context explicitly declares xsd:decimal as the quantity serialization, and the current candidate provides no replacement datatype constraint.","expected":"The qudt:value representation must use the declared canonical xsd:decimal datatype while expressing the source-required value.","suggestion":"Restore sh:datatype xsd:decimal on the qudt:value property shape and retain the value constraint.","evidence_excerpt":""canonical_literal_encoding": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal", "scope": "Declared quantity serialization; no new global ontology range or numeric-equality solution""},{"issue_id":"15023d32ef4e138f598d31ef4c3a982295fdfdca099dbe6b85f7da8173d184d2","category":"SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR","source_clause":"I2.2.5","exact_source_excerpt":"I2.2.5 The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where
         the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.","exact_candidate_excerpt":"sh:node [
                    a sh:NodeShape ;
                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue
                ]","reason":"The candidate removes the constraints requiring the quantity value 7 and the unit DEG, together with their minCount constraints. QuantityValue class membership alone does not enforce the required numeric value or angular unit.","expected":"A QuantityValue node must be present with value 7 and unit DEG.","suggestion":"Restore the qudt:value and qudt:unit property shapes with minCount 1, sh:hasValue "7"^^xsd:decimal, and sh:hasValue unit:DEG.","evidence_excerpt":"Schema term: shellInclinationAngle has parentOrRange http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue, unitIri http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG, and unitSymbol "deg"."}],"change_assessments":[{"change_id":"93acfdfdc5e6aab001d6036a9270a7f1840d5574f86c99728fbe65d87d8d869","disposition":"REGRESSION","exact_source_excerpt":"I2.2.5 The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where
         the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.","previous_excerpt":"sh:node [
                    a sh:NodeShape ;
                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;
                    sh:property [
                        sh:path qudt:value ;
                        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;
                        sh:hasValue "7"^^xsd:decimal ;
                        sh:minCount 1
                    ] ;
                    sh:property [
                        sh:path qudt:unit ;
                        sh:hasValue unit:DEG ;
                        sh:minCount 1
                    ]
                ]","candidate_excerpt":"sh:node [
                    a sh:NodeShape ;
                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue
                ]","reason":"The change removes the nested value and unit property shapes, eliminating enforcement of the source-required 7-degree shell inclination."},{"change_id":"d188b42d0a0b569fdcb53a423cd0303dc37e596b81dd4fd0598f3ab3459e4686","disposition":"REGRESSION","exact_source_excerpt":"I2.2.5 The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where
         the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.","previous_excerpt":"sh:path qudt:value ;
                        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;
                        sh:hasValue "7"^^xsd:decimal ;
                        sh:minCount 1","candidate_excerpt":"sh:node [
                    a sh:NodeShape ;
                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue
                ]","reason":"The change removes the xsd:decimal datatype constraint from qudt:value. The declared quantity encoding requires canonical xsd:decimal serialization, and the candidate provides no replacement constraint."},{"change_id":"15023d32ef4e138f598d31ef4c3a982295fdfdca099dbe6b85f7da8173d184d2","disposition":"REGRESSION","exact_source_excerpt":"I2.2.5 The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where
         the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.","previous_excerpt":"sh:path qudt:value ;
                        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;
                        sh:hasValue "7"^^xsd:decimal ;
                        sh:minCount 1
                    ] ;
                    sh:property [
                        sh:path qudt:unit ;
                        sh:hasValue unit:DEG ;
                        sh:minCount 1","candidate_excerpt":"sh:node [
                    a sh:NodeShape ;
                    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue
                ]","reason":"The change removes the required value equality, unit equality, and cardinality constraints. The remaining class constraint only identifies a QuantityValue and does not encode 7 degrees."}],"reconciliations":[],"unchecked":["Other requirements in UR I2 outside clause I2.2.5 were not assessed.","Independent verification of the source interpretation and SHACL processor behavior was not performed.","Applicability to particular ships or hull configurations beyond the supplied clause was not assessed."]}

